/*! \mainpage preC-SUMO Developer Guide

\tableofcontents

\section intro Introduction
preC-SUMO is the coupling-side adapter between D-FlowFM and C-SUMO in a preCICE setup.

Current core responsibilities are:
- read and validate C-SUMO settings,
- register preCICE meshes and data channels,
- receive far-field data from preCICE and write FF2NF input files,
- wait for and read NF2FF output files,
- convert NF2FF results to connected source/sink writes for D-FlowFM via preCICE.

\section workflow Core Workflow
The implementation follows the main sequence in \ref pre_c_sumo::run. The flow reads settings,
receives ambient data, writes FF2NF input, waits for NF2FF results, converts the near-field
output to connected source/sink entries, and then writes the final coupling data to D-Flow FM via preCICE.

\dotfile preC_SUMO_Swimlanes.dot "preC-SUMO core coupling workflow (current implementation)"

\section architecture Architecture Overview
The system-level picture shows the surrounding coupled components: D-Flow FM, the preCICE adapter,
C-SUMO, and the NF2FF/FF2NF exchange files.

\image html FM-C-SUMO_scheme_precice.drawio.svg "Coupled FM/C-SUMO architecture via preCICE" width=1000px

The more detailed data-mapping view shows how the configuration data is transformed into the
1D arrays used by the preCICE exchange buffers.

\image html "preC-SUMO data mapping diagram-3D Mapping.drawio.svg" "3D data mapping" width=900px

